{
  "identity": {
    "text": "Yes. We need two loaves of bread, one bag of rice, three packets of soup and one liter of juice. Let us take a basket.\n\nEach loaf has a price of two pounds fifty. Two loaves cost five pounds in total. The rice is six pounds for the bag.\n\nEach packet costs two pounds. The quantity is three, so that is six pounds. The juice is two pounds.\n\nThat leaves an amount of sixteen pounds to pay. We can afford it and save nine pounds from our budget.\n\nOf course. We should get four pounds back. If the assistant gives us a coin, we will count it with the notes.\n\nNo. It is expensive, and the hall already has cups. A cheap extra is still unnecessary if we do not need it.\n\nLet us join the queue and then take the food to the hall. We can tell the others exactly how much we spend.",
    "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
    "rate": "-15%",
